# Line endings are declared here rather than left to each machine's core.autocrlf, so a checkout is
# the same on Windows, macOS and Linux. Every blob in this repository is already LF and so is every
# working copy, so this changes no bytes; what it stops is git reporting a file as modified purely
# because autocrlf would have written it back with CRLF. That noise ran to over a hundred files and
# hid real changes among them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts run on macOS and Linux; keep them LF regardless of the Windows checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf
